   "source": [
    "# Week 10: Talking to a Large Language Model\n",
    "\n",
    "**Grade band:** 6 to 8  |  **Duration:** 60 minutes  |  **Platform:** JupyterLite (browser, no account) or Google Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to use this notebook:** run each cell from top to bottom with Shift + Enter. Read the text, run the code, then complete the challenge cells marked **YOUR TURN**. Save your work at the end of the session (File > Download) so it can be uploaded to your portfolio."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f3c8aef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hook: The model that finishes your sentence\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Once upon a ...\" Your brain filled in *time*. A large language model (LLM) does that billions of times, one word at a time, using patterns from an enormous amount of text. Today you send it messages from Python, give it a personality, and catch it making things up.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Please note:** this lesson sends text to an AI service on the internet. Never include your full name, address, school name, or passwords in a prompt."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9d64c0ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Setup: run this cell first.\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# If a data file is not found next to this notebook (for example on Google Colab),\n",
    "# it is loaded from the Wize data folder online instead. Replace this URL after publishing.\n",
    "DATA_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wizeacademy/ml-ai-6-8/main/notebooks/data/\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def load(name):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Load a Wize dataset by file name, from the local data folder or from the web.\"\"\"\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return pd.read_csv(\"data/\" + name)\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        return pd.read_csv(DATA_URL + name)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Setup complete. pandas and matplotlib are ready.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a185215",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Teach 1: Calling an AI from Python\n",
    "\n",
    "Our program builds a web address with the question attached, sends it, and reads the answer back. The `ask_ai` function hides the details so you can focus on the prompt."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "80637e8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import urllib.parse\n",
    "\n",
    "def ask_ai(prompt):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Send a prompt to a free text AI and return its reply. Works in JupyterLite and Colab.\"\"\"\n",
    "    url = \"https://text.pollinations.ai/\" + urllib.parse.quote(prompt)\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        from pyodide.http import open_url          # inside a browser (JupyterLite)\n",
    "        return open_url(url).read()\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        import urllib.request                       # normal Python (Colab, laptop)\n",
    "        req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"User-Agent\": \"Wize-Student-Bot/1.0\"})\n",
    "        return urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=60).read().decode(\"utf-8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(ask_ai(\"Say hello to a middle school coding class in one sentence.\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4fcffad0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Teach 2: Prompts are instructions, personas are prompts\n",
    "\n",
    "The model does exactly what the words ask, so **clear prompts get clear answers**. A **persona** is a prompt that sets the character before the user's question.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept checkpoint:** which prompt will get a better answer: \"penguins\" or \"Explain in two sentences why penguins cannot fly, for a 12 year old\"?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c53da295",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "persona = \"You are a cheerful robot tour guide at an aquarium. Answer in two short sentences. \"\n",
    "question = \"Why can't penguins fly?\"\n",
    "print(ask_ai(persona + question))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6f8ec4f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Teach 3: The model is not always right\n",
    "\n",
    "LLMs predict likely words; they do not look things up. That means they can **hallucinate**: state something false with total confidence. Run the cell, then check the answer against a source you trust."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "89835967",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(ask_ai(\"In one sentence, who won the FIFA World Cup in 2030?\"))\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(ask_ai(\"How many letters are in the word 'strawberry'? Answer with just the number.\"))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0c62ff52",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## YOUR TURN: Challenge\n",
    "\n",
    "**Timer suggestion: 25 minutes.**\n",
    "\n",
    "### Mild\n",
    "Write three different personas for the same question and compare the answers. Which persona gave the most useful answer?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Medium\n",
    "Build a chatbot loop: keep asking the user for input until they type `quit`, and send every message with your persona attached. Add a friendly welcome and goodbye.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Spicy\n",
    "Build a **fact checker game**: ask the model five questions you already know the answers to (from your science or history class), score how many it got right, and print a percent accuracy. Then rewrite one prompt to make the model more accurate and test again."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1193d769",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# MILD: three personas, one question\n",
    "question = \"What should I eat before a soccer game?\"\n",
    "personas = [\n",
    "    \"You are a strict nutrition coach. \",\n",
    "    # TODO: add two more personas\n",
    "]\n",
    "for p in personas:\n",
    "    print(\"PERSONA:\", p)\n",
    "    print(ask_ai(p + question))\n",
    "    print(\"-\" * 40)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a96b9b90",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# MEDIUM: chatbot loop\n",
    "persona = \"You are a friendly study buddy for middle school students. Keep answers under three sentences. \"\n",
    "print(\"Study Buddy is here. Type quit to leave.\")\n",
    "while True:\n",
    "    message = input(\"You: \")\n",
    "    # TODO: if message is \"quit\", print a goodbye and break\n",
    "    # TODO: otherwise print ask_ai(persona + message)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "82bc9f0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# SPICY: fact checker game\n",
    "quiz = [\n",
    "    (\"What is the chemical symbol for water? Answer with the symbol only.\", \"H2O\"),\n",
    "    # TODO: add four more (question, correct answer) pairs you already know\n",
    "]\n",
    "correct = 0\n",
    "for question, answer in quiz:\n",
    "    reply = ask_ai(question)\n",
    "    # TODO: check if answer.lower() is in reply.lower(); if so add 1 to correct\n",
    "    print(question, \"->\", reply.strip())\n",
    "print(\"Accuracy:\", round(correct / len(quiz) * 100), \"%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
